    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0424" n="415" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg415"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.00 Revolutions/601: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Vargas to
                        President Roosevelt</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-05-14">May 14, 1938</date>.<lb/>[Received 8:14
                        p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I take satisfaction in thanking you for the terms of your message, Eminent
                    Friend, who well interprets the spirit of solidarity of American nations at the
                    moment when the advocates of foreign doctrines attempted a coup against
                    Brazilian democracy. I reciprocate, and renew to Your Excellency the assurance
                    of my highest esteem.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Getulio Vargas</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
